				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h2>Repair or Replace? How to Decide</h2>
<p>Consider replacement if your system is over 15 years old, requires frequent repairs, has lost efficiency, uses R-22 refrigerant (being phased out), or repair costs exceed 50% of replacement value.</p></div>
			</div><div class="et_pb_with_border et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_10 mini-head et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h2>Understanding SEER Ratings</h2>
<p>SEER (Seasonal Energy Efficiency Ratio) measures cooling efficiency — higher numbers mean better efficiency and lower energy costs. Modern systems require a minimum 14 SEER. A higher-SEER system costs more upfront but can meaningfully lower monthly cooling bills over the life of the equipment, especially in a climate like North Texas where the AC runs hard for much of the year.</p></div>
			</div>
